# Test: a respawn the plugin declares it cannot meet stops ze at startup
#
# The configuration asks for `respawn true`. The plugin declares
# failure-policy ignore, which says it must not be started again. Ze cannot
# honor both, and the owner settled which way that goes: "if a plugin declare
# that it can not restart then we can not start" (2026-09-06).
#
# The refusal has to name BOTH sides. An operator reading only "ze cannot start"
# does not know whether to edit the configuration or change the plugin.
#
# VALIDATES: AC-7 -- the daemon does not start, and the message names the
# plugin, the policy it declared and the leaf the configuration wrote.
# PREVENTS: ze picking a side in silence. Honoring the leaf would restart a
# plugin whose author forbade it; honoring the declaration would leave what the
# operator wrote with no effect at all, which is the defect this spec was
# written about.

tmpfs=ze-bgp.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external failure-disagree {
		run "ze-test fixture plugin/failure-policy-disagree"
		encoder json
		respawn true;
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze start ze-bgp.conf:timeout=30s
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:pattern=plugin .*failure-disagree.* declares failure-policy .*ignore
expect=stderr:contains=its configuration block asks for respawn
expect=stderr:contains=stopping ze because a plugin failed
reject=stderr:contains=OK: the plugin process was started again
